Body:
realize this is an older issue but we have had `permissions` for a while, docs here: https://opencode.ai/docs/permissions/

in your opencode.json put:
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permission": {
    "edit": "ask",
  }
}
```

And it will give option to review edits before they take place

This is ollama telling you the model doesn't support tools, if you wanna talk to it in opencode you need to set `tool_call` to false so that opencode knows it doesn't support tools

Example:
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "ollama": {
      "models": {
        "deepseek-coder-v2:16b": {
          "tool_call": false
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

```

